    "filed": "2009-05-26",
    "published": "2010-03-03",
    "where": "China",
    "abstract": "The invention provides a method for manufacturing a semiconductor element, which can maintain the equivalent oxide thickness by reducing the thickness of an interface layer in a gate structure. The method includes forming an interface layer on a substrate; a gate dielectric layer such as a high-k dielectric formed on the interfacial layer; a getter layer is formed on the interface layer over the substrate, the getter layer having the function of gettering oxygen from the interface layer, allowing the thickness of the interface layer to be reduced and/or limiting the growth of the interface layer. The invention is beneficial to controlling the equivalent oxide thickness of the grid structure. Wherein the gettering layer may comprise a dielectric and/or a metal layer, which may be removed from the gate stack or remain in the structure.",
