    "published": "2018-11-23",
    "where": "China",
    "abstract": "本发明提供一种改进永磁同步电机控制性能的方法，包括步骤：S1：向一改进的负载转矩观测器输入当前转矩电流和当前机械转速，获得补偿机械转速和负载转矩；S2：将所述补偿机械转速和所述负载转矩输入一改进的积分滑膜控制器，对转矩电流进行补偿获得补偿后的转矩电流。本发明的一种改进永磁同步电机控制性能的方法，可节约系统成本，增加系统的稳定性，同时提高了系统的响应速度和抗扰动性，减小了系统的抖振。 The present invention provides a method for improving the control performance of a permanent magnet synchronous motor, comprising the steps of: S1: inputting the current torque current and the current mechanical speed to an improved load torque observer to obtain the compensated mechanical speed and load torque; S2: The compensated mechanical rotational speed and the load torque are input into an improved integral sliding film controller, and the torque current is compensated to obtain the compensated torque current. The method for improving the control performance of the permanent magnet synchronous motor of the present invention can save the cost of the system, increase the stability of the system, improve the response speed and anti-disturbance of the system, and reduce the chattering of the system.",
    "claims": [
      "1. A method of improving the control performance of a permanent magnet synchronous motor comprising the steps of: s1: inputting the current torque current and the current mechanical rotating speed to an improved load torque observer to obtain a compensated mechanical rotating speed and a load torque; s2: inputting the compensated mechanical rotating speed and the load torque into an improved integral sliding mode controller, and compensating the torque current to obtain a compensated torque current; the expression of the improved load torque observer includes: wherein, ω ismIndicating mechanical speed, TlRepresenting load torque, J representing moment of inertia, b representing damping coefficient, TeRepresents an electromagnetic torque; α, β represent desired poles; the expression of the improved integral sliding mode controller is as follows: s＝c∫edt+e＝cx1+x2 (6)； wherein iqRepresenting compensated torque current, NpThe method comprises the following steps of (a) representing the pole pair number of a motor, wherein lambda represents a permanent magnet rotor flux linkage, a represents a first speed change approaching term coefficient, epsilon represents a second speed change approaching term coefficient, and e represents a mechanical rotating speed error; c represents an integral sliding mode coefficient, rho represents the maximum positive value of the action range of the Y(s) function, delta represents the gradient factor of the Y(s) function, and k represents an exponential approach term coefficient."
    ],
