    "where": "United States",
    "abstract": "A method and structure providing a high-voltage transistor (HVT) including a gate dielectric, where at least part of the gate dielectric is provided within a trench disposed within a substrate. In some aspects, a gate oxide thickness may be controlled by way of a trench depth. By providing the HVT with a gate dielectric formed within a trench, embodiments of the present disclosure provide for the top gate stack surface of the HVT and the top gate stack surface of a low-voltage transistor (LVT), formed on the same substrate, to be substantially co-planar with each other, while providing a thick gate oxide for the HVTs. Further, because the top gate stack surface of HVT and the top gate stack surface of the LVT are substantially co-planar with each other, over polishing of the HVT gate stack can be avoided.",
    "claims": [
      "1. A method, comprising: forming a gate dielectric layer in a trench within an active region of a substrate, the active region being free of any shallow trench isolation feature, the trench having a first depth, and the gate dielectric layer having a top surface that is level with a top surface of the substrate; forming another gate dielectric layer over the gate dielectric layer, the another gate dielectric layer disposed outside the trench; and forming a source region and a drain region within the substrate and on either side of the trench, wherein the source region and the drain region extend into the substrate a second depth greater than the first depth.",
      "2. The method of claim 1, wherein the trench has a first width along a plane parallel to the top surface of the substrate, and wherein the trench has a second width along a plane parallel to a bottom surface of the trench, wherein the second width is less than the first width.",
      "3. The method of claim 2, wherein the gate dielectric layer and the another gate dielectric layer form part of a gate stack of a transistor disposed within the active region, and wherein the first width is substantially equal to a width of the gate stack of the transistor.",
      "4. The method of claim 1, further comprising: after forming the another dielectric layer, forming a metal gate layer over the another dielectric layer.",
      "5. The method of claim 1, further comprising: after forming the gate dielectric layer and prior to forming the another gate dielectric layer, performing a chemical mechanical polishing process to remove excess material of the gate dielectric layer and to planarize the top surface of substrate.",
      "6. The method of claim 4, further comprising: after depositing the another gate dielectric layer and prior to forming the metal gate layer, forming a high-k dielectric layer over the another gate dielectric layer.",
      "7. The method of claim 4, further comprising: prior to forming the metal gate, forming a polysilicon layer over the another gate dielectric layer.",
      "8. The method of claim 7, further comprising: patterning the polysilicon layer to form a patterned polysilicon layer, patterning the another gate dielectric layer to form a patterned another gate dielectric layer, removing the patterned polysilicon layer, and forming the metal gate layer over the patterned another gate dielectric layer.",
      "9. The method of claim 4, wherein the gate dielectric layer, the another gate dielectric layer and the metal gate layer form part of a high-voltage transistor (HVT) disposed within the active region.",
      "10. A method, comprising: forming a first transistor within a first active region of a substrate, the first transistor having a first gate stack; and forming a second transistor within a second active region of the substrate, the second transistor having a second gate stack, and the first and second active regions free of any shallow trench isolation feature; wherein an oxide layer of the first gate stack extends into the substrate.",
      "11. The method of claim 10, wherein a first height of the first gate stack is greater than a second height of the second gate stack.",
      "12. The method of claim 10, wherein a top surface of the first gate stack is level with a top surface of the second gate stack.",
      "13. The method of claim 10, further comprising: forming a first source/drain region within the substrate adjacent to the first gate stack, wherein the oxide layer of the first gate stack extends into the substrate by a first depth, and wherein the first source/drain region extends into the substrate a second depth greater than the first depth.",
      "14. The method of claim 13, further comprising: forming a second source/drain region within the substrate adjacent to the second gate stack, wherein the second source/drain region extends into the substrate a third depth less than the second depth.",
      "15. The method of claim 10, wherein the forming the first transistor having the first gate stack further comprises: forming a trench within the first active region of the substrate; and forming the oxide layer of the first gate stack within the trench.",
      "16. The method of claim 10, wherein forming the first transistor further includes forming a high-voltage transistor (HVT) within the first active region of the substrate, and wherein forming the second transistor further includes forming a low-voltage transistor (LVT) within the second active region of the substrate.",
      "17. A method comprising: forming a transistor within an active region of a substrate, the active region being free of any shallow trench isolation feature, wherein forming the transistor includes: forming a trench, within the active region, filled with a first oxide layer having a top surface level with a top surface of the substrate; and forming a gate electrode over the first oxide layer; wherein a bottom surface of the first oxide layer is spaced a first distance from the top surface of the substrate, the first distance less than a second distance between the top surface of the substrate and a bottom surface of an adjacent source or drain feature of the transistor.",
      "18. The method of claim 17, further comprising: prior to forming the gate electrode, forming a second oxide layer over the first oxide layer, the second oxide layer disposed outside the trench; and forming the gate electrode over the second oxide layer.",
      "19. The method of claim 17, wherein first oxide layer and the gate electrode form part of a first gate stack of the transistor, the first gate stack having a first height that is greater than a second height of a second gate stack of another transistor disposed in an adjacent active region of the substrate.",
      "20. The method of claim 19, wherein top surfaces of the first gate stack and the second gate stack are level with each other."
    ],
