    "where": "United States",
    "abstract": "A FinFET device and a method of forming the same are disclosed. In accordance with some embodiments, a FinFET device includes a substrate having at least one fin, a gate stack across the at least one fin, a strained layer aside the gate stack and a silicide layer over the strained layer. The strained layer has a boron surface concentration greater than about 2E20 atom/cm3 within a depth range of about 0-5 nm from a surface of the strained layer.",
    "claims": [
      "1. A FinFET device, comprising: a substrate having at least one fin; a gate stack across the at least one fin; a strained layer aside the gate stack and having a boron surface concentration greater than about 2E20 atom/cm3 within a depth range of about 0-5 nm from a surface of the strained layer; and a silicide layer over the strained layer.",
      "2. The FinFET device of claim 1, wherein the boron surface concentration of the strained layer is in a range from about 2E20 to 1E21 atom/cm3.",
      "3. The FinFET device of claim 1, wherein the boron surface concentration of the strained layer is in a range from about 1E21 to 5E21 atom/cm3.",
      "4. The FinFET device of claim 1, further comprising a lightly doped region between the gate stack and the strained layer.",
      "5. The FinFET device of claim 4, wherein a first portion of the lightly doped region has a boron surface concentration greater than a second portion of the lightly doped region, and the first portion is located within a depth range of about 0-5 nm from a surface of the lightly doped region, and the second portion is located below the first portion.",
      "6. A FinFET device, comprising: a substrate having at least one fin; a gate stack across the at least one fin; a strained layer aside the gate stack; and a shallow doped region in a surface portion of strained layer, wherein a concentration of the shallow doped region is higher than a concentration of the strained layer, and the shallow doped region and the strain layer have a same conductivity type dopant.",
      "7. The FinFET device of claim 6, wherein the shallow doped region comprises a p-type dopant.",
      "8. The FinFET device of claim 7, wherein the p-type dopant comprises boron.",
      "9. The FinFET device of claim 6, further comprising a lightly doped region aside the strained layer.",
      "10. The FinFET device of claim 9, wherein the shallow doped region has a tailing doping profile laterally extending toward the lightly doped region.",
      "11. The FinFET device of claim 9, wherein the shallow doped region and the lightly doped region have a same conductivity type dopant.",
      "12. The FinFET device of claim 6, wherein the shallow doped region has a depth of less than about 20 nm.",
      "13. The FinFET device of claim 6, further comprising a spacer aside the gate stack and covering the shallow doped region.",
      "14. The FinFET device of claim 6, further comprising a silicide layer over the shallow doped region.",
      "15. The FinFET device of claim 14, further comprising at least one connector disposed on and connected to the silicide layer.",
      "16. A FinFET device, comprising: a substrate having at least one fin; a metal gate stack across the at least one fin; a source and drain region aside the metal gate stack; a lightly doped region between the source and drain region and the metal gate stack; and a shallow doped region in surface portions of the source and drain region and the lightly doped region, wherein the source and drain region, the shallow doped region and the lightly doped region have a same conductivity type dopant; and wherein a concentration of the shallow doped region is higher than a concentration of the source and drain region below the shallow doped region.",
      "17. The FinFET device of claim 16, further comprising a silicide layer covering a portion of the shallow doped region.",
      "18. The FinFET device of claim 17, further comprising a spacer aside the metal stack and covering another portion of the shallow doped region and the lightly doped region.",
      "19. The FinFET device of claim 16, wherein the source and drain region comprises a strained layer.",
      "20. The FinFET device of claim 16, wherein the same conductivity type dopant comprises boron."
    ],
