    "abstract": "The present disclosure relates to an integrated circuit (IC) and a method of formation. In some embodiments, a low voltage region and a high voltage region are integrated in a substrate. A low voltage transistor device is disposed in the low voltage region and comprises a low voltage gate electrode and a low voltage gate dielectric separating the low voltage gate electrode from the substrate. A first interlayer dielectric layer is disposed over the substrate surrounding the low voltage gate electrode and the low voltage gate dielectric. A high voltage transistor device is disposed in the high voltage region and comprises a high voltage gate electrode disposed on the first interlayer dielectric layer.",
    "claims": [
      "1. An integrated circuit (IC), comprising: a low voltage region and a high voltage region integrated in a substrate; a low voltage transistor device disposed in the low voltage region and comprising a low voltage gate electrode and a low voltage gate dielectric separating the low voltage gate electrode from the substrate; a first interlayer dielectric layer disposed over the substrate surrounding the low voltage gate electrode and the low voltage gate dielectric; and a high voltage transistor device disposed in the high voltage region and comprising a high voltage gate electrode disposed on the first interlayer dielectric layer.",
      "2. The IC of claim 1, wherein the high voltage transistor device further comprises an oxide component disposed between the first interlayer dielectric layer and the substrate.",
      "3. The IC of claim 2, wherein the oxide component contacts an upper surface of the substrate.",
      "4. The IC of claim 2, wherein the low voltage gate dielectric comprises an oxide component of the same material and thickness of the oxide component of the high voltage transistor device.",
      "5. The IC of claim 2, wherein the high voltage transistor device further comprises a high-k dielectric component disposed between the oxide component and the first interlayer dielectric layer.",
      "6. The IC of claim 5, wherein the low voltage gate dielectric comprises a high-k dielectric component of the same material and thickness of the high-k dielectric component of the high voltage transistor device.",
      "7. The IC of claim 2, wherein the high voltage transistor device further comprises a high-k dielectric component disposed between the oxide component and the substrate.",
      "8. The IC of claim 2, further comprising a sidewall spacer disposed along sidewalls of the low voltage gate dielectric and the oxide component of the high voltage transistor device.",
      "9. The IC of claim 8, further comprising a hard mask disposed on the low voltage gate electrode and contacting top surfaces of the sidewall spacer.",
      "10. The IC of claim 1, wherein the first interlayer dielectric layer is a low-k dielectric material.",
      "11. The IC of claim 1, wherein the high voltage gate electrode is disposed within a second interlayer dielectric layer that overlies the first interlayer dielectric layer.",
      "12. The IC of claim 11, further comprising a first metal line disposed within the second interlayer dielectric layer and coupled to the low voltage gate electrode through a first contacting via.",
      "13. The IC of claim 12, wherein the first metal line has a bottom surface aligned with that of the high voltage gate electrode.",
      "14. The IC of claim 1, wherein the low voltage gate electrode is a metal gate electrode.",
      "15. An integrated circuit (IC), comprising: a low voltage region and a high voltage region integrated in a substrate; a low voltage transistor device disposed in the low voltage region and comprising a low voltage gate electrode and a low voltage gate dielectric separating the low voltage gate electrode from the substrate; a high voltage transistor device disposed in the high voltage region, the high voltage transistor device comprising a high voltage gate electrode and a high voltage gate dielectric separating the high voltage gate electrode from the substrate; and a first interlayer dielectric layer disposed over the substrate surrounding the low voltage transistor device and the high voltage transistor device; wherein the first interlayer dielectric layer has an upper surface coplanar with a top surface of the low voltage gate electrode and a lower surface coplanar with a first component of the high voltage gate dielectric.",
      "16. The IC of claim 15, wherein the first component of the high voltage gate dielectric comprises an oxide component disposed over the substrate.",
      "17. The IC of claim 16, wherein the first component of the high voltage gate dielectric further comprises a high-k dielectric component disposed over the oxide component.",
      "18. The IC of claim 17, wherein the low voltage gate dielectric comprises a high-k dielectric component of the same material and thickness of the high-k dielectric component of the high voltage transistor device.",
      "19. An integrated circuit (IC), comprising: a low voltage region and a high voltage region integrated in a substrate; a low voltage transistor device disposed in the low voltage region and comprising a low voltage gate electrode and a low voltage gate dielectric separating the low voltage gate electrode from the substrate; a first interlayer dielectric layer disposed over the substrate surrounding the low voltage transistor device; and a high voltage transistor device disposed in the high voltage region, the high voltage transistor device comprising a high voltage gate electrode and a high voltage gate dielectric separating the high voltage gate electrode from the substrate; and a second interlayer dielectric layer overlying the low voltage gate electrode and extended between the high voltage gate electrode and the substrate.",
      "20. The IC of claim 19, wherein the first interlayer dielectric layer has an upper surface coplanar with a top surface of the low voltage gate electrode and a lower surface coplanar with a first component of the high voltage gate dielectric."
    ],
