    "abstract": "An integrated circuit is provided having a system clock and a clock filter. The clock filter has a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of the integrated circuit and for causing the clock filter to block output of the system clock if the sensed temperature is below or above a predetermined temperature.",
    "claims": [
      "1. An integrated circuit comprising: a system clock; a clock filter connected to the system clock; and; logic circuitry for receiving a clock output from the system clock via the clock filter, wherein the clock filter has a temperature sensor for sensing a temperature of the integrated circuit and wherein the clock filter is configured to block the clock output of the system clock to the logic circuitry if the sensed temperature is below or above a predetermined temperature.",
      "2. An integrated circuit according to claim 1, wherein the predetermined temperature is selected such that a temperature-related frequency of the system clock output that is not due to the clock filter is within a predetermined frequency range.",
      "3. An integrated circuit according to claim 2, wherein the predetermined frequency range is within an operating frequency of the logic circuitry."
    ],
