    "abstract": "The alignment mark and method for making the same are described. In one embodiment, a semiconductor structure includes a plurality of gate stacks formed on the semiconductor substrate and configured as an alignment mark; doped features formed in the semiconductor substrate and disposed on sides of each of the plurality of gate stacks; and channel regions underlying the plurality of gate stacks and free of channel dopant.",
    "claims": [
      "1. A semiconductor structure, comprising: a semiconductor substrate having a device region and an alignment region; a plurality of gate stacks formed on the semiconductor substrate in the alignment region and configured as an alignment mark, wherein the plurality of gate stacks include a first gate stack and a second gate stack; doped features formed in the semiconductor substrate and disposed on sides of each of the plurality of gate stacks, wherein the doped features include a source/drain feature continuously extending within the semiconductor substrate from an edge of the first gate stack to an edge of the second gate stack, wherein the doped features have a refractive index of about 3; and channel regions underlying the plurality of gate stacks and free of well dopant, the well dopant being located in the device region.",
      "2. The semiconductor structure of claim 1, wherein the plurality of gate stacks each includes a high-k dielectric material layer and a metal layer disposed on the high-k dielectric material layer.",
      "3. The semiconductor structure of claim 1, wherein the doped features include light doped drain (LDD) features.",
      "4. The semiconductor structure of claim 1, wherein the doped features include heavily doped source/drain (S/D) features.",
      "5. The semiconductor structure of claim 1, wherein the doped features include pocket implantation features.",
      "6. The semiconductor structure of claim 1, wherein the plurality of gate stacks are configured as a grating structure.",
      "7. The semiconductor structure of claim 1, further comprising a field-effect device (FET) in the device region, the FET including: a metal gate formed on the semiconductor substrate; source and drain regions formed in the semiconductor substrate and disposed on sides of the metal gate; and a channel doping feature formed in a FET channel region and underlying the metal gate.",
      "8. The semiconductor structure of claim 7, wherein the channel doped feature in the FET channel region includes channel doped species for adjusting threshold voltage and the channel region in the alignment region is free of channel doping species.",
      "9. The semiconductor structure of claim 1, wherein the semiconductor substrate includes silicon.",
      "10. A semiconductor structure having an alignment mark, comprising: a semiconductor substrate having a device region and an alignment region; a field-effect device formed within the device region, including: a first gate stack formed on the semiconductor substrate; a first source and drain regions formed in the semiconductor substrate and disposed on both sides of the first gate stack; and a first channel region having a channel doped feature formed in the semiconductor substrate and underlying the gate stack; and an alignment mark formed within the alignment region, including: a second gate stack and a third gate stack formed on the semiconductor substrate; a second source and drain region formed in the semiconductor substrate and continuously extending within the semiconductor substrate from an edge of the second gate stack to an edge of the third gate stack; and a second channel region free of channel doped feature in the semiconductor substrate and underlying the second gate stack, and wherein the semiconductor substrate includes silicon and the second source and drain regions have a refractive index of about 3.",
      "11. The semiconductor structure of claim 10, wherein the first gate stack includes a high-k dielectric material layer and a metal layer disposed on the high-k dielectric material layer; and the second gate stack includes the high-k dielectric material layer and the metal layer disposed on the high-k dielectric material layer.",
      "12. The semiconductor structure of claim 10, wherein the first gate stack includes a high-k dielectric material layer and a metal layer disposed on the high-k dielectric material layer; and the second gate stack includes a silicon oxide layer and a polysilicon layer disposed on the silicon oxide layer.",
      "13. The semiconductor structure of claim 10, wherein the first and second source and drain regions include: light doped drain (LDD) features; and heavily doped source/drain (S/D) features.",
      "14. The semiconductor structure of claim 10, wherein the channel doped feature includes doped species incorporated for adjusting threshold voltage.",
      "15. The semiconductor structure of claim 10, wherein the second gate stack includes a high-k dielectric material layer and a metal layer disposed directly on the high-k dielectric material layer such that the metal layer physically contacts the high-k dielectric material layer.",
      "16. A method comprising: providing a semiconductor substrate having a device region and an alignment region; performing a first ion implantation to the semiconductor substrate within the device region while the alignment region is covered by an implantation mask layer; thereafter forming a first polysilicon gate stack in a device region and a second polysilicon gate stack in an alignment region; thereafter performing a second ion implantation to the semiconductor substrate within the device region and within the alignment region, wherein performing the second ion implantation modifies a refractive index of the semiconductor substrate and increases a wafer quality of an alignment signal from the alignment region to be greater than 1%; and replacing the first and second polysilicon gate stacks with metal gate stacks.",
      "17. The method of claim 16, further comprising: forming an interlayer dielectric (ILD) material layer on the semiconductor substrate; coating a photoresist layer on the ILD material layer; aligning a mask to the semiconductor substrate according to an alignment signal from the alignment region; and exposing the photoresist layer using the mask having a contact pattern.",
      "18. The method of claim 16, wherein the first ion implantation includes ion implantations selected from the group consisting of well implantation, threshold voltage implant, and a combination thereof.",
      "19. The method of claim 16, wherein the second ion implantation includes n-type light-doped drain (n-LDD) doping process with doping dose greater than about 1014 ions/cm2.",
      "20. The method of claim 16, wherein performing the second ion implantation forms a doped region in the semiconductor substrate having a refractive index of about 3."
    ],
