    "inventors": [
      "Yun Jing Lin",
      "Wei-Han Fan",
      "Yu-Hsien Lin",
      "Yimin Huang"
    ],
    "filed": "2014-05-20",
    "published": "2014-09-04",
    "where": "United States",
    "abstract": "The present disclosure describes a method of fabricating semiconductor device including providing a semiconductor substrate and a gate stack disposed on the semiconductor substrate. A first spacer element is formed on the substrate abutting the first gate stack. In an embodiment, a source/drain region is then formed. A second spacer element is then formed is adjacent the first spacer element. The second spacer element has a second height from the surface of the substrate, and the first height is greater than the second height. In embodiments, the second spacer element is used as an etch stop in forming a contact to the source/drain region.",
    "claims": [
      "1. A method for making a semiconductor device comprising: providing a gate stack on a semiconductor substrate; forming a first spacer element abutting the gate stack; forming a source region and a drain region in the semiconductor substrate adjacent the gate stack after forming the first spacer element; forming a silicon oxide layer on the semiconductor substrate after forming the source and drain regions; and etching the silicon oxide layer to provide a second spacer element including a first sidewall and a second sidewall, wherein the first sidewall abuts the first spacer element and wherein the second sidewall abuts a raised source/drain region.",
      "2. The method of claim 1, further comprising: depositing an inter layer dielectric (ILD) on the substrate; and etching the ILD to form a via, wherein the etching the ILD using the second spacer element as an etch stop; and forming a contact in the via.",
      "3. The method of claim 2, wherein the contact has a physical interface with the second spacer element.",
      "4. The method of claim 1, wherein the first sidewall of the second spacer element is longer than the second sidewall of the second spacer element.",
      "5. The method of claim 1, further comprising: forming a contact etch stop layer (CESL) on the semiconductor substrate, wherein the CESL has a first region interfacing a lateral sidewall of the first spacer element and a second region interfacing a lateral sidewall of the second spacer element.",
      "6. The method of claim 1, wherein the forming the source and drain regions includes epitaxially growing the source and drain regions.",
      "7. The method of claim 1, wherein the forming the source and drain regions includes doping a region of the semiconductor substrate.",
      "8. The method of claim 1, wherein the forming the source and drain regions includes forming a strained region in the semiconductor substrate.",
      "9. The method of claim 8, wherein the forming the second spacer element includes depositing a silicon oxide layer on the semiconductor substrate and anisotropically etching the silicon oxide layer to form the second spacer element.",
      "10. The method of claim 1, further comprising: forming a contact connected to the raised source/drain region, wherein the contact includes an interface with the second spacer element.",
      "11. A method of fabricating a semiconductor device, comprising: providing a gate stack disposed on a semiconductor substrate; forming a first spacer element abutting the gate stack; forming a source/drain in the substrate adjacent the gate stack; and after forming the source/drain, forming a second spacer element including a first sidewall and a second sidewall, wherein the first sidewall abuts the first spacer element and wherein the second sidewall abuts a raised source/drain region.",
      "12. The method of claim 11, further comprising: forming a contact connected to the raised source/drain region, wherein the contact includes an interface with the second spacer element.",
      "13. The method of claim 11, further comprising: forming a silicide layer on the source/drain, wherein the silicide layer includes an interface with the second spacer element.",
      "14. The method of claim 13, wherein the forming the silicide layer is performed prior to the forming the second spacer element.",
      "15. The method of claim 11, wherein the forming the source/drain includes epitaxially growing the source/drain.",
      "16. A method comprising: forming a gate stack on a substrate; forming a first spacer element abutting the gate stack, wherein the first spacer element has a first height from a surface of the substrate; depositing a dielectric material on the substrate and anisotropically etching the dielectric material to form a second spacer element adjacent the first spacer element, wherein the second spacer element has a second height from the surface of the substrate, and the first height is greater than the second height; depositing a contact etch stop layer having an interface with each of the first and second spacer elements; and using the second spacer element as an etch stop when forming a contact to a source/drain region of the substrate adjacent the gate stack.",
      "17. The method of claim 16, wherein the contact has a lateral interface with the second spacer element.",
      "18. The method of claim 16, further comprising: forming the source/drain region after forming the first spacer element and prior to forming the second spacer element.",
      "19. The method of claim 18, wherein the forming the source/drain region includes forming a silicon germanium (SiGe) feature in the substrate.",
      "20. The method of claim 18, further comprising: forming a silicide region on the source/drain region, wherein the silicide region has a lateral interface with the second spacer element."
    ],
