    "abstract": "A method of fabricating a semiconductor integrated circuit (IC) is disclosed. The method includes receiving a semiconductor device, patterning a first hard mask to form a first recess in a high-resistor (Hi-R) stack, removing the first hard mask, forming a second recess in the Hi-R stack, forming a second hard mask in the second recess in the Hi-R stack. A HR can then be formed in the semiconductor substrate by the second hard mask and a gate trench etch.",
    "claims": [
      "1. An integrated circuit (IC) structure, comprising: a semiconductor substrate; and a resistor stack disposed over the semiconductor substrate, the resistor stack including: a first dielectric layer disposed over the semiconductor substrate; a gate material layer disposed over the first dielectric layer; metal layers disposed over the first dielectric layer and on sides of the gate material layer; and a dielectric stack disposed over the gate material layer, an interlayer dielectric (ILD) layer having a first portion disposed adjacent the resistor stack and a second portion disposed directly on top of the dielectric stack above the gate material layer, wherein an upper surface of the second portion of the ILD layer is substantially coplanar with upper surfaces of the metal layers and an upper surface of the first portion of the ILD layer is substantially coplanar with the upper surface of the second portion of the ILD layer.",
      "2. The IC structure of claim 1, wherein the gate material layer includes a conductive layer.",
      "3. The IC structure of claim 1, wherein the gate material layer includes an amorphous silicon layer.",
      "4. The IC structure of claim 1, wherein an edge of the second portion of the ILD layer aligns with an edge of the gate material layer.",
      "5. The IC structure of claim 1, wherein the metal layers are disposed on sidewalls of the second portion of the ILD layer and sidewalls the gate material layer.",
      "6. The IC structure of claim 1, wherein the metal layers include one material selected from the group consisting of Ti, Ag, Al, TiAlN, TaC, TaCN, TaSiN, Mn, Zr, TiN, TaN, Ru, Mo, Al, WN, Cu, W, and a combination thereof.",
      "7. The IC structure of claim 1, wherein the first dielectric layer includes one material selected from the group consisting of LaO, AlO, ZrO, TiO, Ta2O5, Y2O3, SrTiO3 (STO), BaTiO3 (BTO), BaZrO, HfZrO, HfLaO, HfSiO, LaSiO, AlSiO, HfTaO, HfTiO, (Ba,Sr)TiO3 (BST), Al2O3, Si3N4, oxynitrides (SiON), and a combination thereof.",
      "8. The IC structure of claim 1, further comprising: sidewall spacers formed on sidewalls of the metal layers and on sidewalls of the first dielectric layer.",
      "9. The IC structure of claim 1, further comprising: a transistor stack disposed over the semiconductor substrate, the transistor stack including: a second dielectric layer formed over the semiconductor substrate; a metal gate formed over the second dielectric layer; and sidewall spacers disposed on sidewalls of the metal gate and on sidewalls of the second dielectric layer.",
      "10. The IC structure of claim 9, wherein the portions of the ILD layer is disposed between the resistor stack and the transistor stack, wherein an upper surface of the metal gate is substantially coplanar with the upper surface of the portion of the ILD layer.",
      "11. The IC structure of claim 10, wherein the upper surfaces of the metal layers are substantially coplanar with the upper surface the first portion of the ILD layer.",
      "12. The IC structure of claim 9, wherein the metal layers include substantially similar materials as the metal gate.",
      "13. The IC structure of claim 9, wherein the second portion of the ILD layer includes one material selected from the group consisting of silicon oxide, oxynitride, silicon nitride, and a combination thereof.",
      "14. An integrated circuit (IC) structure, comprising: a semiconductor substrate; a resistor stack disposed over the semiconductor substrate, the resistor stack including: a first dielectric layer disposed over the semiconductor substrate; a conductive layer disposed over the first dielectric layer; a dielectric stack disposed over the conductive layer; and metal layers disposed over the first dielectric layer and along sidewalls of the conductive layer; a transistor stack disposed over the semiconductor substrate, the transistor stack including: a second dielectric layer disposed over the semiconductor substrate; a metal gate disposed over the second dielectric layer; and a first portion of an interlayer dielectric (ILD) layer disposed between the resistor stack and the transistor stack and a second portion of the ILD layer is disposed directly on top of the dielectric stack, wherein an upper surface of the second portion of the ILD layer, an upper surface of the first portion of the ILD layer, and an upper surface of the metal layers are substantially coplanar.",
      "15. The IC structure of claim 14, further comprising: first sidewall spacers disposed on sidewalls of the metal layers of the resistor stack; and second sidewall spacers disposed on sidewalls of the metal gate and the second dielectric layer of the transistor stack.",
      "16. The IC structure of claim 14, further comprising: source and drain regions disposed on two sides of the transistor stack.",
      "17. The IC structure of claim 16, wherein the source and drain regions include epitaxially grown strained structures.",
      "18. The IC structure of claim 14, wherein the semiconductor substrate includes an isolation feature.",
      "19. An integrated circuit (IC) structure, comprising: a semiconductor substrate; an input/output high-resistor (IO Hi-R) region including a conductive layer and a dielectric stack disposed on the conductive layer; a field-effect transistor (FET) region including a metal gate; an isolation feature disposed between the IO Hi-R region and the FET region; and a first portion of an interlayer dielectric (ILD) layer disposed over the isolation feature and a second portion of the ILD layer is disposed directly on top of the dielectric stack, wherein an upper surface of the second portion of the ILD layer is substantially coplanar with an upper surface of the metal gate, wherein an upper surface of the first portion of the ILD layer is substantially coplanar with the upper surface of the second portion of the ILD layer, wherein the IO Hi-R region further includes metal layers formed on sidewalls of the conductive layer and the second portion of the ILD layer, and wherein the upper surface of the second portion of the ILD layer is substantially coplanar with upper surfaces of the metal layers."
    ],
