    "abstract": "A transistor includes a gate dielectric structure over a substrate and a work function metallic layer over the gate dielectric structure. The work function metallic layer is configured to adjust a work function value of a gate electrode of the transistor. The transistor also includes a silicide structure over the work function metallic layer. The silicide structure is configured to be independent of the work function value of the gate electrode of the transistor.",
    "claims": [
      "1. A transistor comprising: a gate dielectric structure over a substrate; a first type work function metallic layer over the gate dielectric structure, the first type work function metallic layer being configured to adjust a work function value of a gate electrode of the transistor; a second type work function metallic layer over the first type work function metallic layer; and a silicide structure over the second type work function metallic layer, the silicide structure configured to be independent of the work function value of the gate electrode of the transistor.",
      "2. The transistor of claim 1, wherein the silicide structure is spaced from the gate dielectric structure by a distance of 30 Å or more.",
      "3. The transistor of claim 1, wherein the transistor is free of a diffusion barrier layer between the second type work function metallic layer and the silicide structure.",
      "4. The transistor of claim 1, further comprising a dielectric material around the silicide structure, wherein a top surface of the dielectric material is substantially level with a top surface of the silicide structure.",
      "5. The transistor of claim 1, further comprising a dielectric material around the silicide structure, wherein a top surface of the silicide structure is over a top surface of the dielectric material.",
      "6. The transistor of claim 1, wherein the gate dielectric structure comprises a high-k dielectric layer.",
      "7. The transistor of claim 6, wherein the gate dielectric structure further comprises an interfacial layer.",
      "8. The transistor of claim 1, further comprising spacers adjacent to the gate dielectric structure, wherein the first type work function metallic layer is between the spacers and the silicide structure.",
      "9. An integrated circuit comprising: an N-type transistor comprising: a first gate dielectric structure over a substrate; a first n-type work function metallic layer over the first gate dielectric structure, the first n-type work function metallic layer being configured to adjust a work function value of a gate electrode of the N-type transistor; and a first silicide structure over the first n-type work function metallic layer, the first silicide structure configured to be independent of the work function value of the gate electrode of the N-type transistor; and a P-type transistor comprising: a second gate dielectric structure over the substrate; a p-type work function metallic layer over the second gate dielectric structure, the p-type work function metallic layer being configured to adjust a work function value of a gate electrode of the P-type transistor; a second n-type work function metallic layer over the p-type work function metallic layer; and a second silicide structure over the second n-type work function metallic layer, the second silicide structure configured to be independent of the work function value of the gate electrode of the P-type transistor.",
      "10. The integrated circuit of claim 9, wherein the second silicide structure is spaced from the second gate dielectric structure by a distance of 30 Å or more.",
      "11. The integrated circuit of claim 9, wherein the P-type transistor is free of a diffusion barrier layer between the second n-type work function metallic layer and the second silicide structure.",
      "12. The integrated circuit of claim 9, further comprising a dielectric material around the first silicide structure and the second silicide structure, wherein a top surface of the dielectric material is substantially level with top surfaces of the first and second silicide structures.",
      "13. The integrated circuit of claim 9, wherein at least one of the first gate dielectric structure or the second gate dielectric structure comprises a high-k dielectric layer.",
      "14. The integrated circuit of 13, wherein the at least one of the first gate dielectric structure or the second gate dielectric structure further comprises an interfacial layer.",
      "15. The integrated circuit of claim 9, wherein the P-type transistor further comprises spacers adjacent to the second gate dielectric structure and the p-type work function metallic layer is between the spacers and the second silicide structure.",
      "16. The integrated circuit of claim 15, wherein the second n-type work function metallic layer is between the spacers and the second silicide structure.",
      "17. The integrated circuit of claim 9, further comprising a dielectric material around the first silicide structure and the second silicide structure, wherein a top surface of the first silicide structure and the second silicide structure is over a top surface of the dielectric material.",
      "18. A transistor comprising: a gate dielectric structure over a substrate; spacers adjacent to the gate dielectric structure; a first work function metallic layer over the gate dielectric structure and along sidewalls of the spacers, the first work function metallic layer being configured to adjust a work function value of a gate electrode of the transistor; a second work function metallic layer over the first work function metallic layer; and a silicide structure over the second work function metallic layer, the silicide structure configured to be independent of the work function value of the gate electrode of the transistor.",
      "19. The transistor of claim 18, wherein the transistor is free of a diffusion barrier layer between the second work function metallic layer and the silicide structure.",
      "20. The transistor of claim 18, further comprising a dielectric material around the silicide structure, wherein a top surface of the dielectric material is substantially level with a top surface of the silicide structure."
    ],
